## Commands & permissions

| Command | Who | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| `/class <player> <ability>` | `empoweredsmp.admin` (op by default) | Permanently assigns an ability + grants its Level 0 kit |
| `/ei` | anyone (no-op unless Prosperity) | Opens the Prosperity extra inventory |
| `/empowered info\|setlevel\|resetdeaths <player> [value]` (aliases: `/esmp`, `/eadmin`) | `empoweredsmp.admin` | View/adjust a player's level or death counter |
| `/unlocknether` / `/unlockend` / `/unlockvillagers` | `empoweredsmp.op` | One-way, irreversible global gates |

Abilities: `PROSPERITY, INVISIBILITY, ELEMENTAL, VITALITY, RANGER, MOBILITY, DEFENSE, STRENGTH`

(Note: "Prosperity" here is one of the eight ability classes, unrelated to the plugin's own name —
both just happen to share a similar theme.)

## Design decisions worth knowing about

Everything numeric (percentages, cooldowns, caps, heart totals) lives in **config.yml** so you
can tune balance without recompiling. A few things needed interpretation since the spec didn't
give exact numbers for every step — check config.yml's comments and adjust if my read differs
from what you intended:

- **Vitality hearts by level**: I used {0:11, 1:11, 2:13, 3:16}, anchored on the spec's explicit
  "Heart Surge restores to 16 hearts at level 3." Levels 1-2 are my best-fit interpolation.
- **Level Fragment / Level Upgrader materials**: plain vanilla items with custom names only (as
  you asked) — Prismarine Shard and Nether Star respectively — tagged internally so they can't be
  faked by a normal prismarine shard/nether star. Change `LEVEL_FRAGMENT_MATERIAL` /
  `LEVEL_UPGRADER_MATERIAL` constants in `EmpoweredSMP.java` if you'd rather use different
  base items.
- **"Netherite Spear" / "Diamond Spear" (Mobility)**: vanilla Minecraft has no Spear item type.
  I substituted a Trident tagged "Lunge Spear" with a custom right-click lunge ability (15s
  cooldown) to approximate the Level 0 kit and the "Lunge 3" mechanic. If you have a separate
  custom-items plugin/datapack that adds real spears, tell me and I'll wire the restrictions to
  that item type instead of the Trident stand-in.
- **Full Invis at Invisibility L3**: vanilla `InvisibilityEffect` already hides armor and held
  items from other players' view of the entity model, so no extra packet work was needed for
  that part. What isn't automatic is *forcing* it on below 4 hearts with a distinct cooldown from
  the permanent L1 invisibility — that's handled via a temporary effect layered on top.
- **Hero of the Village**: implemented as the real vanilla `HERO_OF_THE_VILLAGE` potion effect
  (amplifier 4 = "level V", amplifier 9 = "level X"), which is the actual mechanic that discounts
  villager trades in vanilla Minecraft — no custom price math needed.
- **Enforcement model**: item/enchant/potion restrictions are enforced by cancelling the
  interact/click/consume/pickup event when a player doesn't qualify. This catches items from
  `/give`, other plugins, or trading, but a determined player could still briefly hold a
  disallowed item in an unopened container; nothing engages until they try to use or move it.
- **Data storage**: per-player YAML files under `plugins/EmpoweredSMP/playerdata/`, as
  discussed — fine for a single server, would need a rewrite to MySQL for a BungeeCord/Velocity
  network sharing player state across servers.

## Things you'll likely want to extend

- The custom crossbow with Quick Charge X (Ranger L2) and the "Infinity OR Mending, chosen each
  time you hold a bow" (Ranger L1) aren't implemented yet — both need a small `PlayerItemHeldEvent`
  /custom-crossbow-item listener that I can add next; I stopped short of guessing your preferred
  UX for the "choose each time" toggle (a right-click menu? sneak+swap?).
- Prosperity's "choose any 2 Netherite tool types" at L2 (vs. "all of them" at L3) currently only
  gates *whether* any netherite tool is usable at L2, not which specific 2 — I'd want to know how
  you want that chosen (a GUI, a command, automatically the first 2 equipped) before building it.

Happy to keep building out either of those, or adjust any of the interpretation calls above.
